  "bio": "Matthew R. Morgan’s Texas family roots date back nearly 200 years ago. Matt’s ancestral family moved to Texas with Stephen F. Austin, as part of the original 300 in 1825. Stephen F. Austin is considered the founder of Texas as we know it today. Matt graduated from Sam Houston State University in Huntsville with a bachelor’s degree in business. Matt received two separate job offers; one was from an elite stock brokerage firm, and the other from a well-known insurance company. This was the pinnacle moment in Matt’s career, for he picked the profession that would help others when they experienced a loss. Matt is proud of being an Eagle Scout and was the recipient of the Young American Award. In 1993, he earned proclamation of a day in his honor through.",
